From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Burke Cates <burke.cates@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM: drm/msm/dp: don't tear the link down again after a failed enable

Commit 1bda647ce61b ("drm/msm/dp: move link-level teardown from
display_disable to display_unprepare") moved off_link and the PHY exit
from msm_dp_display_disable() into msm_dp_display_unprepare() and says
SST behaviour is unchanged. It is not for a failed .atomic_enable():
msm_dp_display_disable() returned early on !power_on, so after link
training gave up, .atomic_post_disable() only dropped the runtime PM
reference. Now msm_dp_display_unprepare() runs msm_dp_ctrl_off_link()
unconditionally, on a mainlink that msm_dp_ctrl_on_link()'s failure path
(deinitialize_mainlink) already took down: link clocks off, PHY powered
off and re-initialised. off_link then reads and writes MAINLINK_CTRL
with the link clocks off.

On the ASUS Zenbook A16 (glymur) eDP training gave up after all
attempts, and the next CRTC disable (an fbdev blank) reset the SoC
silently within 0.3 s. Restore the old behaviour: skip the link
teardown when power_on is false.

Fixes: 1bda647ce61b ("drm/msm/dp: move link-level teardown from display_disable to display_unprepare")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
Not-for-upstream: local workaround for one laptop, not reviewed for
  submission; use only for local testing.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1685,6 +1685,17 @@
 {
 	struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display = &dp->msm_dp_display;
 
+	/*
+	 * A failed .atomic_enable() (link training gave up) leaves power_on
+	 * false, and on_link's failure path has already taken the mainlink
+	 * down: its clocks off, the PHY powered off. Tearing the link down
+	 * again touches the link registers with their clocks off, which on
+	 * glymur ends in a silent SoC reset. Before the link teardown moved
+	 * here, msm_dp_display_disable() skipped it on !power_on; keep that.
+	 */
+	if (!msm_dp_display->power_on)
+		goto out;
+
 	/* dongle is still connected but sinks are disconnected */
 	if (dp->link->sink_count == 0)
 		msm_dp_link_psm_config(dp->link, &dp->panel->link_info, true);
@@ -1699,6 +1710,7 @@
 
 	msm_dp_display->power_on = false;
 
+out:
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(&msm_dp_display->pdev->dev);
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "type=%d Done\n", msm_dp_display->connector_type);
